From 1261111b60ec75763887b8dad7b41cd9d382d7d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erhan Bilgili <erhan.bilgili@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 00:31:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Fall back to linear dma-buf images.

Use exportable linear images for opaque R8G8B8A8 swapchains when DRM
format modifiers are unavailable. Verify RADV's OPAQUE_FD export is a
dma-buf before publishing it.

(cherry picked from commit 1261111b60ec75763887b8dad7b41cd9d382d7d4)

GE-Proton adaptation: this base has no managed-swapchain color space, no
consumer wake eventfd, and keeps caps_flags before the modifier arrays in
vk_select_managed_modifiers(); the layout plumbing was inserted around
those differences. managed_create_image() is otherwise identical to the
upstream result.

Source: https://github.com/nanomatters/wine-salkim/commit/1261111b60ec75763887b8dad7b41cd9d382d7d4
---
 dlls/win32u/vulkan.c | 255 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 179 insertions(+), 76 deletions(-)

